[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775002430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115192#issuecomment-3775002430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115192","id":3775002430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hAfc-","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T21:19:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T21:19:40Z","body":"Hello! I'm the one who added `has_static_method()` in #82767. By \"the next compat breakage\", I most likely meant 5.0, since we prefer not to introduce breaking changes in minor versions without sufficient justification.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775002430/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775028054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115192#issuecomment-3775028054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115192","id":3775028054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hAltW","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T21:26:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T21:30:42Z","body":"Hi @dalexeev I'm not aware of any issue doing this in 4.7. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately, right now the `has_method` is completely broken and does not function as expected from GDExtension. If folks would rather keep `has_static_method` as is and just change `has_method`, I am open to that since there is technically no overlap with `Object` for `has_static_method`.\r\n\r\nThe other option is we leave `has_method` and just introduce `has_script_method` as a short-term gap closer to address the limitations in GDExtension. Would that be a viable alternative for 4.7 @AThousandShips ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775028054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775122978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115192#issuecomment-3775122978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115192","id":3775122978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hA84i","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T21:53:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T21:58:03Z","body":"> Unfortunately, right now the `has_method` is completely broken and does not function as expected from GDExtension.\r\n\r\nI'm not quite sure what you mean by \"completely broken\". You can still use `Script.get_script_method_list()` to get script methods without the base native methods (though it's a bit inconvenient since there's no [`no_inheritance` parameter](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/80418), but you can exclude inherited methods from base script like [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/78c6632eb174aabb2790975cf83e28fee065b43d/editor/scene/connections_dialog.cpp#L1564-L1580)).\r\n\r\nIf you want to add the `Script.has_script_method()` method, similar to `Script.has_script_signal()`, to avoid getting a list of all methods via `Script.get_script_method_list()`, then you don't need to rename the virtual method `ScriptExtension._has_method()` to implement this functionality. Yes, this is still a confusing naming convention, but it doesn't pose any technical problems.\r\n\r\nAlso, I don't think we should expose the static counterpart. This method exists internally, but for a public API, it's probably enough that static methods are present in the shared method list, and you can check `METHOD_FLAG_STATIC` in the method metadata. If absolutely necessary, we could add `Script.has_script_static_method()` and `ScriptExtension._has_static_method()` and thereby temporarily preserve the current naming scheme, for consistency with `ScriptExtension._has_method()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775122978/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775181131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115192#issuecomment-3775181131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115192","id":3775181131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hBLFL","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T22:08:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T22:08:17Z","body":"> I'm not quite sure what you mean by \"completely broken\". You can still use `Script.get_script_method_list()` to get script methods without the base native methods (though it's a bit inconvenient since there's no [`no_inheritance` parameter](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/80418), but you can exclude inherited methods from base script).\r\n\r\nI am already doing this, but it doesn't address the corner case of knowing when a method defined in a parent class is overridden in the subclass due to the lack of the no inheritance parameter.\r\n\r\n> If you want to add the `Script.has_script_method()` method, similar to `Script.has_script_signal()`, to avoid getting a list of all methods via `Script.get_script_method_list()`, then you don't need to rename the virtual method `ScriptExtension._has_method()` to implement this functionality. Yes, this is still a confusing naming convention, but it doesn't pose any technical problems.\r\n\r\nUsing `ScriptExtension._has_method` isn't sufficient. While this would work if I were only concerned with the `has_method` functionality of my own scripts implemented in my extension, it wouldn't work when I am inspecting scripts defined in other languages, like GDScript. For that to work, something needs to exist on `Script`, right @dalexeev ?\r\n        \r\n> Also, I don't think we should expose the static counterpart. This method exists internally, but for a public API, it's probably enough that static methods are present in the shared method list, and you can check `METHOD_FLAG_STATIC` in the method metadata.\r\n\r\nThat's a fair point, and I can certainly remove the static counterpart changes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775181131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775236408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115192#issuecomment-3775236408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115192","id":3775236408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hBYk4","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T22:24:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T22:24:55Z","body":"@dalexeev I went ahead and scaled back the change to focus solely on adding the `has_script_method` helper for scripting access, leaving everything else as is to avoid any disruptions in API.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3775236408/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"per